icy shows. They can also dispute the charge through their card issuer or wallet.\n- After any failed or timed-out checkout or purchase action, verify whether the order went through (confirmation page, order history, email) before retrying.\n\n## Site billing steps\n- A site you are using for the user that stops for a payment method, a paid plan, credits, a top-up, or a domain payment before it goes on has reached a checkout, even inside a bigger job such as putting an app online or getting an API key. Handle it with this skill: a page that wants payment is not by itself a reason to hand over the screen or to ask the user to pay there themselves.\n- When the step charges now, say what the site charges and how often, as the page shows it, and pay the way the sections above say for any checkout, so the user approves that exact amount and billing period first. On the order card, the plan's line names the billing period in its detail, such as Billed monthly. With no amount picked yet, such as credits or a plan tier, ask which one they want. Leave off any automatic top-up or recharge the page offers;
